iwlwifi: skip iwl_dealloc_ucode() on the firmware load failure path

Without firmware, iwl_req_fw_callback() always ends on its failure path.
Upstream frees drv->fw there since ab07506b0454; that path later needed
fixes for a use-after-free (bea2662e7818) and a double-free (353d321f63f7).

Replaces the reverts added in package-helpers bf3b68a1 (2022-05-14):
  001  revert of 6518f83ffa51, obsolete since 3d913719df14
  002  revert of ab07506b0454
  003  revert of bea2662e7818, only needed for 002 to build

'failure' is never true, so iwl_req_fw_callback() compiles to the same
code as with 002+003. drv->fw is still freed by iwl_drv_stop().

Without firmware nothing is allocated in drv->fw, so nothing leaks. With a
firmware file that fails after partial parsing, what it allocated may
leak, as with 002+003.

